Certainly, I can help you with that! To avoid repeating the `iframe` part in all lines, I will assume you have multiple sources for the `src` attribute and we will use a JavaScript approach. Here's a code snippet:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <style>
    .video-container {
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
  </style>
  <script>
    function generateIframe(src) {
      var iframe = document.createElement("iframe");
      iframe.src = src;
      iframe.width = "560";
      iframe.height = "315";
      iframe.frameBorder = "0";
      iframe.allow = "accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture";
      iframe.allowFullscreen = true;

      return iframe;
    }

    function appendIframes() {
      var sources = [
        "https://www.youtube.com/embed/ABCDEFGHIJ",  // Replace with your desired sources
        "https://www.youtube.com/embed/KLMNOPQRST"
        // Add more sources as needed
      ];

      var container = document.getElementById("iframe-container");

      sources.forEach(function(src) {
        var div = document.createElement("div");
        div.className = "video-container";
        div.appendChild(generateIframe(src));
        container.appendChild(div);
      });
    }
  </script>
</head>
<body onload="appendIframes()">
  <div id="iframe-container"></div>
</body>
</html>
```

This code snippet will generate and append the `iframe` elements to the specified element with the ID `iframe-container` and thus avoid repeating the `iframe` part. You can modify the `sources` array to add more video sources as needed.

