To determine whether an Android device is low-end, you can check for the device's hardware specifications, such as the CPU speed, RAM size, and GPU performance. Here's a method that checks for these specifications and determines whether the device is low-end:
```java
public boolean isLowEndDevice() {
    // Get the device's hardware specifications
    int cpuSpeed = getCpuSpeed(); // in MHz
    int ramSize = getRamSize(); // in MB
    int gpuPerformance = getGpuPerformance(); // in MHz

    // Define thresholds for low-end devices
    int lowEndCpuSpeedThreshold = 1000;
    int lowEndRamSizeThreshold = 512;
    int lowEndGpuPerformanceThreshold = 100;

    // Check if the device is low-end based on the hardware specifications
    return (cpuSpeed < lowEndCpuSpeedThreshold || ramSize < lowEndRamSizeThreshold || gpuPerformance < lowEndGpuPerformanceThreshold);
}

// Helper methods to get the device's hardware specifications
