chosen:
The issue you are experiencing might be related to the fact that you are not properly updating the `currentRating` variable before entering the event listener logic. You can solve this issue by updating `currentRating` right after getting the rating from the `node.querySelector('button').title * 20` expression.

Here is the modified logic inside `stash.addEventListener("page:scene", async function() {` (I've added comments to the lines I've changed):

```javascript
let sceneId = updateSceneId();
waitForElementClass("rating-stars", function () {
  const n = document.getElementsByClassName('rating-stars')[1];
  let node = n.cloneNode(true);

  waitForElementByXpath("//div[contains(@class, 'VideoPlayer')]", function(xpath, el) {
    if (!document.getElementById('video-stars')) {
      const control = el.querySelector('.vjs-control-bar');
      node.setAttribute('id', 'video-stars');
      control.appendChild(node);
      control.insertBefore(node, control.childNodes[9]);
    }

    // Get current set rating or if on first pass get rating from HTMl
    let rating = currentRating || node.querySelector('button').title * 20;

    // Update currentRating here (added line)
    currentRating = rating;

    console.log("xpath rating: " + rating);

    // The rest of the code remains the same
    //...
  });
});
```

This should ensure that the `currentRating` variable is properly updated, and the event listeners will use the most up-to-date rating value for all subsequent interactions.

